  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nDuring an initial sync of my massive account, I saw this appearing as synapse was marking /sync requests as processed (25 minutes later).\r\n```\r\n2018-05-24 20:04:04,376 - synapse.rest.client.v2_alpha.sync - 348 - WARNING - GET-80775- Event '$15038575302050923rSTmh:matrix.org' is under room u'!cURbafjkfsMDVwdRDQ:matrix.org' instead of '!liSMaPmhIAVOyCHhdT:matrix.org'\r\n2018-05-24 20:04:04,379 - synapse.rest.client.v2_alpha.sync - 348 - WARNING - GET-80775- Event '$15038575562051193NuSGj:matrix.org' is under room u'!cURbafjkfsMDVwdRDQ:matrix.org' instead of '!DgvjtOljKujDBrxyHk:matrix.org'\r\n2018-05-24 20:04:04,382 - synapse.rest.client.v2_alpha.sync - 348 - WARNING - GET-80775- Event '$15018848482433138yGYPS:matrix.org' is under room u'!cURbafjkfsMDVwdRDQ:matrix.org' instead of '!ZjJkQNQAlmRlGyyPSZ:matrix.org'\r\n2018-05-24 20:04:04,389 - synapse.rest.client.v2_alpha.sync - 348 - WARNING - GET-80775- Event '$15038574582050065gMgtB:matrix.org' is under room u'!cURbafjkfsMDVwdRDQ:matrix.org' instead of '!PJuJrAtZEvdTHLxoWr:matrix.org'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe interesting thing is it seems to be related to whatever the sync pulls up. For instance, an hour or two later I stopped getting the first 3 warnings and was only seeing the last one.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce (maybe)\r\n\r\n* Have a big account\r\n* Try and do a fresh /sync over and over\r\n* Wait for warnings\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: t2l.io\r\n- **Version**:        0.29.1\r\n- **Install method**: pip\r\n- **Platform**:       Ubuntu 16.04 lxc container on an Ubuntu 16.04 host",
